<speak>
<s>This is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">02082026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Iran's foreign ministry has petitioned the UN Security Council, invoking Article Fifty-One self-defence — and it names a naval blockade, not the airstrikes, as the violation it's answering.</s> <s>A blockade is itself an act of war under customary law once declared and enforced, and it stops neutral shipping carrying fuel, food and medicine for ninety million people.</s> <s>Washington hasn't confirmed a blockade exists... which leaves the most consequential measure in this war unnamed by the state conducting it.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>President Trump says he's cancelled a planned strike on Iran because a framework for a deal was agreed — but he made that cancellation conditional on a rapid final agreement.</s> <s>A conditional cancellation is a deadline attached to a use of force, where the party setting the condition also judges whether it's been met.</s> <s>Saudi Arabia, Qatar, Türkiye and Pakistan pressed for the pause, and not out of sympathy for Tehran — their refineries, airspace, desalination plants and expatriate workforces all sit inside the blast radius of any retaliation.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Three bills now sit before the US Congress that would designate Sudan's Rapid Support Forces a terrorist organisation.</s> <s>Washington already determined in January of last year that the RSF committed genocide and sanctioned its commander Hemedti — whose sanctioned brother was received in Washington anyway, months later.</s> <s>No matching bill touches the United Arab Emirates, credibly accused of arming and financing the militia, and a war economy running on gold and gum arabic doesn't clear through banks that read American lists.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's Rangers shot dead two brothers in a single village in Azad Kashmir, during an eight-week protest movement over electoral reform.</s> <s>A communications blackout now covers Sunday's second-phase Assembly vote, disabling polling-agent reporting, result transmission, journalists' filing and ambulance dispatch all at once.</s> <s>Amnesty put July's toll at forty, and a shutdown is the one intervention that degrades the evidence of every other intervention — so allegations of rigging become unfalsifiable in both directions.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A woman carried an improvised explosive device into a pavement cafe on Kudrinskaya Square in central Moscow on Saturday evening, killing three people.</s> <s>A guard's tackle limited the toll, and Russia's Investigative Committee has opened a terrorism case — but no party has claimed the attack.</s> <s>Whoever the state names as responsible will decide what surveillance powers and movement controls follow for Moscow's residents.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In India's Assam, six people have gained citizenship under a law written for an estimated five hundred thousand.</s> <s>The Citizenship Amendment Act requires an applicant to first declare themselves a foreign migrant, forfeiting any claim they already hold by birth or descent.</s> <s>Tens of thousands of cases still sit before Foreigners Tribunals, where the burden of proof falls on the person, not the state.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Aerodiana sightseeing aircraft crashed minutes after takeoff over Peru's Nazca Lines, killing all thirteen people aboard.</s> <s>Regulators have grounded and reinstated that desert route repeatedly since two thousand and eight.</s> <s>Peru's civil aviation authority hasn't yet said what caused Saturday's crash.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>In Gaza, Israeli strikes killed Palestinians two days after a disarmament agreement was reached.</s> <s>Hamas's weapons hand-over is a countable, one-way act that can be photographed; Israel's withdrawal is a phased schedule that Israel alone certifies as complete.</s> <s>No body has been named to verify a single withdrawal phase — and an agreement with only one verifiable side isn't symmetric, whatever it says on paper.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>India has moved its entire petrol supply to a twenty percent ethanol blend without giving buyers a choice at the pump, and a survey found sixty-seven percent of drivers report lower mileage.</s> <s>Ethanol carries about a third less energy per litre, so a household paying the same rupees for fewer kilometres is absorbing a price rise that never appears in the price.</s> <s>Brazil ran this experiment for forty years — but built a flex-fuel fleet first, and the sequencing is the whole difference between a policy and a levy.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa's food inflation has fallen to a sixteen-year low, cushioned by maize yields of six point four tonnes per hectare.</s> <s>Decades of adoption of modified seed and precision farming built a yield buffer that absorbed an oil shock which normally pushes food prices up with it.</s> <s>Egypt, Pakistan and Nigeria face the same shock without that buffer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers in London estimate the pandemic cut global output by six point three two percent in twenty twenty.</s> <s>Every figure of that kind rests on a counterfactual — a growth path the model invents, because the world where the pandemic didn't happen was never observed.</s> <s>What the panel of forty-six countries did find is that higher debt and stricter lockdowns predicted larger losses, and higher vaccination rates smaller ones.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Ten American embassies across the Middle East have told citizens to consider leaving.</s> <s>War-risk insurers reprice cargo cover and traders price a Hormuz shutdown the moment such alerts post — so an advisory moves money before it moves anyone.</s> <s>The State Department hasn't designated this an ordered departure, which is the legal trigger for evacuation flights.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Ebola has now killed one thousand five hundred and eighty-seven people out of three thousand six hundred and five confirmed cases in the Democratic Republic of Congo.</s> <s>Licensed vaccines target the Zaire strain; this outbreak is Bundibugyo, which they aren't proven to stop.</s> <s>The <sub alias="World Health Organization">WHO</sub> says containment needs far more resources — in provinces where armed conflict blocks contact tracing altogether.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Researchers at the Indian Institute of Technology in Gandhinagar have built a fluorescent stain that reveals a plant's xylem in minutes.</s> <s>Conventional dyes need harsh fixation that distorts the tissue and bind too broadly to read clearly; this one binds a specific cell-wall target on living tissue.</s> <s>Xylem is the plumbing that decides how a plant survives drought — and the instrument that lets you measure a trait usually arrives before the trait can be bred for, in sorghum, millet, rice and wheat across South Asia, God willing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A spacecraft sent to rescue NASA's Swift observatory now needs rescuing itself.</s> <s>Katalyst's Link vehicle lost two of its three reaction wheels and began tumbling on multiple axes, cutting its power and blocking commands mid-mission.</s> <s>Engineers have halved the spin rate, and a capture attempt depends on whether they can halt it entirely.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A single typed sentence made Google Earth's new AI feature place a nuclear plant in Iran that doesn't exist.</s> <s>Open-source investigators verify claims by cross-referencing satellite imagery against shadows, known structures and capture timestamps — a technique that works only because convincing fakes used to be expensive.</s> <s>The lasting damage isn't that a false image gets believed; it's that a true one — a razed village in Darfur, a demolished street in Gaza — can now be waved away, and doubt always favours whoever's holding the bulldozer.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Galaxy Research has traced three sweeps that drained four thousand five hundred and eighty-five offline bitcoin wallets, worth eighty-nine million dollars, without any of them ever going online.</s> <s>The suspected flaw is predictable key generation on Coldcard-made keys, not stolen hardware — meaning the money was gone the moment the key was created.</s> <s>The blockchain can't show whether one attacker or several are behind it, and the vendor hasn't answered.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Michigan has confirmed nine water systems breached, joining thirty in Minnesota, with federal agencies saying seven states were hit and declining to name the rest.</s> <s>Officials blame Iranian hackers who exploited remote-access tools rather than any failure in treatment itself.</s> <s>No contamination's been reported — but a utility that learns of an intrusion from Washington isn't watching its own network.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>